_model: standard-page
---
title: PyCon Trademark & Satellite Event Policy
---
body:

PyCon DE 2027 is a community conference. It is organised by the non-profit Python Software Verband e.V. (PySV) and made possible by volunteers, speakers, sponsors, and attendees who put in their time, money, and work every year.
The name, the logo, and the reputation of this conference were built by that community.
They are not free for anyone to borrow.

## The PyCon Name Is a Trademark

**"PyCon" is a registered trademark of the [Python Software Foundation](https://www.python.org/psf/) (PSF) in the United States (U.S. Reg. No. 4,820,531) and in other jurisdictions.**

The PSF permits the use of the PyCon name only for conferences that focus on Python, are open to the public at a reasonable price, have a code of conduct, and are approved by the PSF Trademarks Committee.
See the [PSF PyCon Trademark Usage Policy](https://www.python.org/psf/trademarks/pycon/) for details.

The names "PyCon DE" and "PyCon DE 2027", the PyCon DE logo, and our visual identity identify the conference organised by PySV.
No one else may use them without our prior written permission.

## We Welcome Satellite Events

Hackathons, sprints, workshops, meetups, and community initiatives around the conference make PyCon DE better.
We actively welcome them, and we are happy to list them in the conference programme and promote them to our attendees, **provided they meet all of the requirements below**.

**To propose a satellite event, use our [Call for Satellite Events](/satellite-events/).**

## What Qualifies as a Satellite Event

A satellite event must meet **every one** of these requirements:

1. **Community first.** The event exists to learn, share, build, or contribute to Python and open source. Its purpose is not lead generation, recruiting, product marketing, or sales.
2. **Open and accessible.** Anyone from the community can attend. It is free or priced to cover costs only. There are no invite-only guest lists for customers or prospects. The venue and format are accessible, and accessibility information is published.
3. **Code of Conduct.** The event adopts and enforces the [PyCon DE Code of Conduct](https://pioneershub.github.io/pyconde-conference/code-of-conduct/), with named contact persons on site.
4. **Inclusive.** The event actively welcomes people of all backgrounds and experience levels, from first-time contributors to core developers.
5. **Transparent.** Organisers, partners, and sponsors are named publicly. Any commercial backing is clearly declared.
6. **Gives back.** The event contributes to the community: open-source work, openly shared material, mentoring, or support for the conference and its programmes such as financial aid.
7. **Approved before it is announced.** The event is proposed through our call, and it is announced only after we confirm it in writing. It complements the conference programme and does not compete with it.
8. **Shared values.** The event reflects the values of the Python community: respect, openness, inclusion, and collaboration.

If an event meets these requirements, we will gladly help it succeed.
If it does not, it is not a PyCon DE satellite event, no matter how it is advertised.

## Free Riders Are Not Welcome

**Let us be absolutely clear: if you plan to run a meetup, party, "side event", or recruiting session timed to the conference week in order to tap into our attendees, our speakers, and our reputation without contributing to the community that makes this conference possible, you are not welcome, and we will act.**

PyCon DE does not run on goodwill alone. Every ticket, sponsorship, and volunteer hour pays for the venue, the financial-aid grants, the recorded talks, and the free programmes that the whole community benefits from.
Riding on that work for free takes from everyone who pays for it.

Companies that want to reach our community have a fair and welcome way to do so: [become a sponsor](/sponsoring/).

## What Counts as Misuse

Any of the following without our prior written permission is unauthorised use:

- Using "PyCon", "PyCon DE", "PyCon DE 2027", our logo, our visual identity, or a confusingly similar name in event titles, ads, listings, domain names, social media handles, hashtags, or job posts.
- Claiming or implying an affiliation with the conference, for example by calling an event "official", a "satellite", a "side event", a "pre-party", an "after-party", or a "fringe event" of PyCon DE, or by advertising it as happening "at" or "around" PyCon DE.
- Promoting an event to our attendees at or near the venue, in conference channels, or by approaching speakers and attendees on our behalf.
- Using names, photos, recordings, or data of our speakers and attendees to promote an event.

## Consequences

We take misuse seriously and we follow through. If we find unauthorised use of our names, logo, or identity, these are the consequences:

1. **Immediate removal.** We will demand that all references be taken down and set a short deadline to comply.
2. **Platform takedowns.** We will report the listing, ads, and accounts to the platforms that host them, such as Meetup, Eventbrite, Luma, LinkedIn, and social networks, under their trademark infringement procedures. This can lead to removed events and suspended accounts.
3. **Notification of the trademark owner.** We will inform the Python Software Foundation, which may take action of its own.
4. **Legal action.** We may send a formal cease-and-desist letter (Abmahnung) through our lawyers, demanding a binding declaration to cease and desist backed by a contractual penalty. Under German law, the infringing party generally bears the legal costs of a justified cease-and-desist letter. We may also seek court injunctions and damages.
5. **Exclusion from the conference.** People and organisations involved may be excluded from sponsorship, speaking, the satellite programme, and attendance at future PyCon DE events.
6. **On-site enforcement.** Unauthorised promotion at the venue is a violation of the house rules and the Code of Conduct. Those responsible will be asked to leave.
7. **Public clarification.** We will publicly state that the event is not affiliated with PyCon DE.

## When in Doubt, Ask First

If you are not sure whether your plans are allowed, ask us before you announce anything.
We would much rather help you build a great community event than deal with misuse after the fact.

- Propose a satellite event: [Call for Satellite Events](/satellite-events/)
- Become a sponsor: [Sponsoring](/sponsoring/)
- Everything else: [contact us](/contact/)
